00:30:28,571 --> 00:30:34,571
Jackass Forever (stylized as jackass fore♥er) is a 2022 American reality slapstick comedy film directed and produced by
Jeff Tremaine, along with producers Spike Jonze and Johnny Knoxville, and was released by Paramount Pictures.

11
00:33:31,428 --> 00:33:37,428
It is the fourth main installment in the Jackass film
series, following Jackass 3D (2010).

12
00:36:34,285 --> 00:36:40,285
The film stars original Jackass members Knoxville, Steve-O, Dave England, Wee Man, Danger Ehren, Chris Pontius, Preston Lacy, as well as newcomers
Sean "Poopies" McInerney, Zach Holmes, Jasper Dolphin, Eric Manaka, Rachel Wolfson, the Jackass film crew, and celebrity guests.

13
00:39:37,142 --> 00:39:43,142
This is the first Jackass film not to feature Ryan Dunn following his death in 2011, and the first without Bam
Margera being a primary cast member as he was fired during production, appearing in only one skit.

14
00:42:40,000 --> 00:42:46,000
Jackass Forever premiered at the Chinese Theatre in Hollywood, California, on
February 1, 2022, and was theatrically released on February 4.

15
00:45:42,857 --> 00:45:48,857
The film was well-received by critics, with many
considering it the best film of the franchise.

16
00:48:45,714 --> 00:48:51,714
It was also a commercial success, grossing over $80 million
worldwide against a budget of $10 million.

17
00:51:48,571 --> 00:51:54,571
Unused footage from the film was compiled separately, titled
Jackass 4.5, and released on Netflix on May 20, 2022.

18
00:54:51,428 --> 00:54:57,428
A sequel is set to release on June 26, 2026.

19
00:57:54,285 --> 00:58:00,285
The film explores themes of pain, disgust, stunt, stuntman, stupidity.

